                <li>✔ <strong>Free Forever:</strong> No trial limitations or subscription requirements.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Common Use Cases for HTML Formatter</h3>
            <p>
                Our HTML Formatter is designed to assist developers, designers, and content managers in multiple scenarios:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Beautifying Copied Code:</strong> Often, HTML copied from tutorials, websites, or emails is messy. Formatting it improves readability and reduces errors.</li>
                <li><strong>Minifying HTML for Production:</strong> Minifying HTML reduces file size, resulting in faster page loads and improved SEO.</li>
                <li><strong>Collaborative Projects:</strong> Multiple developers working on the same codebase need consistent formatting to avoid merge conflicts.</li>
                <li><strong>Learning and Debugging:</strong> Beginners can understand HTML structure more easily when the code is formatted neatly.</li>
                <li><strong>Preparing Templates:</strong> Web designers can create reusable templates with clean, readable code.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Advanced Tips for HTML Formatting</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Use the <strong>Beautify</strong> option during development to maintain a consistent code structure while editing.</li>
                <li>Use the <strong>Minify</strong> option before deploying to production to reduce bandwidth usage and improve load times.</li>
                <li>Combine HTML minification with CSS and JavaScript minification for optimal website performance.</li>
                <li>Keep comments in your development environment for clarity, but remove them in production using the minify feature.</li>
                <li>Validate your HTML code after formatting or minification using online validators to ensure it follows web standards.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h3>

            <p><strong>Q1: Is this HTML Formatter free?</strong></p>
            <p>Yes! Our HTML Formatter is completely free to use with no registration, hidden fees, or trial limitations.</p>

            <p><strong>Q2: Does the tool store my code?</strong></p>
            <p>No. All processing is done in your browser, and your HTML code is never uploaded to our servers. Your data remains private and secure.</p>

            <p><strong>Q3: Can I format very large HTML files?</strong></p>
